# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout while Prettier's
# default (endOfLine: "lf") wants LF — so `npm run format:check` fails on files
# nobody edited, and any operation that re-creates a file (a revert, a branch
# switch, a stash pop) can turn a clean tree red. That is a CI failure with no
# author and no fix in the diff, which is the kind people learn to ignore.
#
# `eol=lf` sets the working-tree ending too, not just the stored one, so the
# checkout matches what the formatter and CI expect on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
